  "description": "DINTUS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H81 Dy4 N3 Ni5 O45,3.67(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.061-3.882 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.44-112.53°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C40H97N3O49Ni5Dy4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 11 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
